<ul class="legend" aria-label="Colour code">
  <% %w[works partial regression fails missing unknown not-tested].each do |state| %>
    <li><span class="swatch cell-<%= state %>"><%= ResultState.glyph(state) %></span> <%= ResultState.words(state) %></li>
  <% end %>
  <li><span class="swatch cell-works cell-tester"><%= ResultState.glyph("works") %></span> tester-verified</li>
  <li><span class="swatch cell-unconfirmed cell-hint-works"><%= ResultState.glyph("works") %></span> community, unconfirmed</li>
</ul>
<p class="legend-note">
  Community reports show up right away, outlined. A cell takes its colour once <%= MatrixCell::AGREEMENT %> or more different machines agree, or at once from a tester's run (framed).
  Orange means it doesn't work although it should on that Mac; red means it's a regression: a tester's earlier run on the same model and stack found it working.
  Blue means it isn't supported yet by Aurora, Asahi or Omarchy.
</p>
